  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: On any other day, the slightly elliptical orbit of the  moon would make
    it look smaller in the distance, only blocking the center of the sun and leaving
    a ring of light, known as an annular eclipse, or the different paths of the sun
    and the moon on our sky would make them slightly misaligned, causing only a partial
    eclipse. But today, everything is perfect. Both spheres, looking exactly the
    same size, completely block the sight of each other, and the sky around them
    is suddenly full of stars. Right behind both is the star cluster of Hyades, the
    nearest cluster to Earth, and you and your team successfully make the necessary
    observations and photographs.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
